Build the AIR compute path as a shared library for the Metal driver.

tools/mesa/air/air_metal.c is air_run's compute path -- a Metal function's LLVM module
through the AIR frontend into a Gallium compute state and a grid on the Adreno -- behind
the contract in tools/mesa/air/air_metal.h, which mentions nothing of NIR, Gallium or
ir3: the Metal driver (userland/src/redwoodmetal.m) must not grow a dependency on Mesa's
headers for it. On the device it is /redwood/lib/libredwoodair.dylib, which is where
-newComputePipelineStateWithDescriptor: will compile the bitcode Metal hands it
(docs/metal.md 10.12).

Both targets are declared here rather than with the rest of the frontend for the reason
air_run already is: they need libgallium, which meson has not defined when
src/compiler/air is read, and they are given air_run's dependencies exactly so that a
driver linking the library gets the path the harness measured.

air_metal_test is that library driven the way the driver will drive it, on softpipe: it
is handed the frontend's include directory and nothing else, so a call air_metal.h fails
to provide shows up as a test that cannot be written.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/meson.build
@@ -335,6 +335,46 @@
   install : false,
 )
 
+# libredwoodair: the same path air_run takes -- a Metal shader through the AIR frontend
+# into a compute state and a grid on the Adreno -- as a shared library, for the Metal
+# driver in userland/src/redwoodmetal.m. Its contract is src/compiler/air/air_metal.h and
+# mentions nothing of Mesa; this is only where it is built, beside air_run and for the
+# same reason, that libgallium exists here and not where the frontend is read. The
+# dependencies are deliberately air_run's: a driver that links this gets the path the
+# harness measured, not a second one assembled for it.
+redwoodair_link_args = []
+if host_machine.system() == 'darwin'
+  # the Metal driver links against this by name, so the name has to be where
+  # tools/mk-mesa.sh installs it on the device
+  redwoodair_link_args += '-Wl,-install_name,/redwood/lib/libredwoodair.dylib'
+endif
+
+libredwoodair = shared_library(
+  'redwoodair',
+  files('../../../compiler/air/air_metal.c'),
+  include_directories : [inc_include, inc_src, inc_mapi, inc_mesa, inc_gallium,
+                         inc_gallium_aux, inc_gallium_winsys_sw, inc_gallium_winsys,
+                         include_directories('../../drivers')],
+  dependencies : [dep_m, idep_air, idep_mesautil, driver_softpipe, driver_freedreno,
+                  dep_libdrm],
+  link_with : [libgallium, libgalliumvl_stub, libws_null, libfreedrenowinsys],
+  link_args : redwoodair_link_args,
+  build_by_default : false,
+  install : false,
+)
+
+# air_metal_test: the library driven the way the driver will drive it, on softpipe. It is
+# given the frontend's include directory and nothing else, so that a call the contract
+# does not provide shows up as a test that cannot be written.
+air_metal_test = executable(
+  'air_metal_test',
+  files('../../../compiler/air/air_metal_test.c'),
+  include_directories : include_directories('../../../compiler/air'),
+  link_with : [libredwoodair],
+  build_by_default : false,
+  install : false,
+)
+
 gmemtool = executable(
   'gmemtool',
   [
